    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `namesakeCount` on owner creation \u2014 the number of existing owners (before the create) sharing the same first and last name, case-insensitively.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `namesakeCount` (int32, `readOnly`, `minimum: 0`) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in responses.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `namesake_count` column field (`Integer namesakeCount`) with getter/setter. It's persisted because the acceptance test reads the value back via `GET /api/owners/{id}` after creation, so it must survive beyond the create request.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, before saving the new owner, compute the count of existing owners whose first and last name match case-insensitively (`countNamesakes` helper using `equalsIgnoreCase`), and set it on the owner. Because it runs over `findAllOwners()` before the new owner is saved, it counts only prior namesakes.\n\n4. **`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb; the others kept consistent).\n\nMapStruct maps the new field automatically by name (Owner \u2194 OwnerDto), so no mapper changes were needed.",
